    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:micro_black_hole_evaporator",
      "title": "Micro Black Hole Evaporator",
      "text": "A black hole lighter than a mountain, held in a cage and fed as fast as it evaporates: it glows with Hawking radiation hotter than any star.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 4$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the hole's mass and how fast it is fed. It radiates at T = \u0127c\u00b3/(8\u03c0GMk): lighter is hotter, and the power grows as 1/M\u00b2. Feed it just what it loses: feed it less and it shrinks, runs away and explodes; more and it swells into the feed. Lighter than 6\u00d710\u2078 kg, its gamma rays are too hot for the shield."
    },
